From f95e116d944496ca2c1dff369c8393514d641d4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (SGR dev session)" <claude@sgr-dev.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 22:12:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ml): VolatilityForecaster.fit() crashed on every real
 GARCH fit + cover module (82% -> 100%)

BUGFIX (production code change - genuine bug found during coverage work):

sgr/ml/volatility_forecaster.py line 122 called
res.conditional_volatility.iloc[-1], assuming a pandas.Series. With
the installed arch version (8.0.0), arch_model().fit() returns
conditional_volatility as a numpy.ndarray, which has no .iloc
attribute. Every real GARCH(1,1) fit therefore crashed with
AttributeError - this was never caught by the ImportError-only
EWMA fallback, so in this environment VolatilityForecaster.fit()
was never actually succeeding via the GARCH path. mypy already
statically flagged this exact issue pre-fix ("Item ndarray... has
no attribute iloc [union-attr]"), confirming it as a genuine,
pre-existing bug rather than a newly introduced one.

Fix: replaced conditional_vol.iloc[-1] with
np.asarray(res.conditional_volatility)[-1], which works correctly
for both pandas.Series and numpy.ndarray, since np.asarray() is a
no-op on an already-ndarray input.

Net effect on mypy sgr/ baseline: 118 -> 117 (one error resolved by
the fix - the flagged union-attr error on this exact line no longer
applies; all other pre-existing errors elsewhere are untouched).

TEST COVERAGE (82% -> 100%):

- Add tests/ml/test_volatility_forecaster.py: 12 tests covering
  sgr/ml/volatility_forecaster.py's VolatilityForecaster.
- fit()/predict() exercised via real GARCH(1,1) maximum-likelihood
  fitting (arch + scipy are installed in this environment) on
  synthetic-but-realistic returns with volatility clustering, rather
  than mocking the arch library - this is what surfaced the bug
  above.
- Covers: too-few-returns ValueError, successful fit + metadata,
  forced-stationarity branch (alpha+beta >= 1.0, via a minimal fake
  arch result object), EWMA fallback when arch is missing
  (sys.modules patch) and _fit_ewma() directly, predict() unfitted
  fallback vs. fitted real forecast, confidence-level-driven interval
  width, lower-bound floor at 0.0, and update()'s no-op-when-unfitted
  vs. variance-adjustment-when-fitted paths.
- Full suite verified green: 1248 passed, 9 skipped, 0 failed.
  Coverage 93.82% -> 94.05%. ruff unchanged (22, pre-existing).
  mypy sgr/ improved 118 -> 117 (see bugfix note above; not a new
  regression baseline, a resolved pre-existing error).
